pr_comments:
@gaudecker In the end, you are just piling hacks over other hacks to make something work that just goes against how the rest of the UI works. It is unnatural and forced.

I think for specifically what this PR aims to solve, property pinning (https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4274) makes far more sense because its entirely general purpose and does not require developers having to write a custom interface for every single type of object you want to have editing more accessible. 

Sure, it does not look "cool" like the drawers, but it gets the job done with orders of magnitude less lines of code to maintain.

